[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186133806 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8b1ca86b-8272-5408-8192-c946c288b937" "question-073aeafa-8770-5a15-8253-20c41456014f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8b1ca86b-8272-5408-8192-c946c288b937" :question/id #uuid "8b1ca86b-8272-5408-8192-c946c288b937" :question/math-academy-id "q-139658" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & {1}^{2} \\\\ 2 & {2}^{2} \\\\ 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ 4 & {4}^{2} \\\\ 5 & {5}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta$ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-96843461-585d-55ec-acb5-913c23f9b3ab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-96843461-585d-55ec-acb5-913c23f9b3ab"